  message: "DONE in PR #952 (merged to dev at c6ba0f1ead).\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. BufferedReader.{readLine,read}, Scanner.{next,nextLine,nextInt},\nInputStream.read and InputStreamReader.read are dual fs_read/ipc_recv rows\nunder call_site_undecidable; java.py stamps io_target_kind by resolving the\nreceiver's last binding and unwrapping the nested-constructor chain, as an\nexplicit bounded loop rather than recursion. InputStream.read was ABSENT\nentirely, so \"InputStream is = System.in; is.read();\" had matched no row.\n\nTWO OF THIS ITEM'S OWN PREMISES WERE WRONG, corrected rather than carried:\n\n(1) \"produces NO untrusted_input source at all\" is TOO STRONG. System.in is\nrowed as an ipc_recv ATTRIBUTE and fires on the module_attr_ref edge. Measured\non a four-method fixture BEFORE the change: fs_read 4 (both the stdin AND the\nfile readers) plus ipc_recv 2 at System.in. The defect was MISCLASSIFICATION at\nthe call that transfers the bytes, not absence.\n\n(2) The item asked to verify the constructor rows FIRST, since an fs_read\nfallback with nothing behind it would leave the stdin crossing represented\nnowhere. Checked, and the answer was not the one anticipated: java emits NO\ncalls edge for object_creation_expression at all, so there are no constructor\nrows and there never could be. The fallback is System.in's attribute row.\nfs_read stays first for that reason; the order is pinned by a test in\ntest_abstention_target_declaration.py, falsified before being kept.\n\nEVIDENCE. Fixture after: fs_read 2 / ipc_recv 4 -- exactly the two stdin reads\nmoved, both file reads unmoved, total unchanged at 6. Corpus A/B (one survey\nand one XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm, diffed both ways) over gatling, clover and\njenkins: +24 chains, 0 REMOVED, 0 MOVED. All 24 are java.io.InputStream.read.\nThe stamp fired 10 times, all in clover (8 host_path, 2 in_memory), and each\nread back correct against source.\n\nTHE NEGATIVE RESULT, which is the honest part: 0 MOVED. Not one receiver in\nthree repositories resolved to a standard stream, so the ipc_recv direction\nthis item exists for is demonstrated ON THE FIXTURE and NOT at corpus scale.\njenkins carries 16 BufferedReader read edges and gatling 2; the stamp fired on\nnone, because every receiver was a field or a parameter, which abstains by\ndesign. Presence reached the rows; reachability did not follow.\n\nBLAST RADIUS IS THREE LANGUAGES: _CATALOG_PARENTS declares kotlin <- java and\nscala <- java, so these rows load for all three. Two of gatling's four added\nchains are in .scala files.\n\nnet_stream is deliberately never stamped: narrowing keeps only rows whose\nboundary equals the resolved one, so a stamp with no matching row would empty\nthe candidate list and DELETE the classification."  # 9d4c
